insert into artikel (slug,judul,judul_en,ringkasan,ringkasan_en,konten,konten_en,kategori,gambar_url,penulis,status,tanggal)
values ('coco-fiber-kerajinan','Coco Fiber untuk Kerajinan Tangan & Dekorasi Rumah','Coco Fiber for Handicrafts & Home Decor Products','Selain untuk kebutuhan industri, tekstur coco fiber yang hangat dan alami menjadikannya bahan baku favorit para pengrajin. Dari keset anyaman dan tali, hingga hiasan dinding dekoratif, seratnya yang kasar namun lentur mengubah limbah sabut kelapa menjadi produk dengan karakter buatan tangan yang khas.','Beyond industrial use, coco fiber''s warm, natural texture makes it a favorite raw material for artisans. From woven doormats and rope to decorative wall hangings, its coarse yet flexible strands turn coconut husk waste into products with genuine handmade character.',
$$ <h2 data-en="Woven Doormats, Rope &amp; Cordage">Keset Anyaman, Tali, dan Cordage</h2><p data-en="Coir fiber has long been spun into rope and twine because of its natural resistance to saltwater and abrasion, historically used in maritime cordage. Today, the same durable strands are woven into doormats and floor mats prized for their coarse, slip-resistant texture, ideal for entryways that see heavy foot traffic. Artisans also braid coir into decorative rope for baskets, plant hangers, and rustic-style furniture accents.">Serat coir sudah lama dipintal menjadi tali dan benang karena sifatnya yang tahan terhadap air asin dan gesekan, dan secara historis dipakai untuk tali-temali kapal laut. Kini, serat yang sama diolah menjadi keset lantai yang disukai karena teksturnya yang kasar dan anti-licin, cocok untuk area pintu masuk dengan lalu lintas tinggi. Pengrajin juga menganyam coir menjadi tali dekoratif untuk keranjang, gantungan tanaman, hingga aksen furnitur bergaya rustic.</p><p data-en="Because the fiber holds dye well while still showing its natural grain, crafters can produce both earthy neutral pieces and vividly colored accent items from the same raw material.">Karena serat ini menyerap pewarna dengan baik namun tetap menampilkan serat alaminya, pengrajin bisa menghasilkan produk bernuansa netral alami maupun aksen warna-warni mencolok dari bahan baku yang sama.</p><h2 data-en="Decorative Panels &amp; Wall Art">Panel Dekoratif &amp; Hiasan Dinding</h2><p data-en="Compressed coir sheets are increasingly used as decorative wall panels in cafes, boutique hotels, and eco-conscious interiors, valued for their organic, textured look that synthetic materials struggle to replicate. Because the material is lightweight and easy to cut, artisans shape it into custom wall art, framed textures, and acoustic panel backing that doubles as both decoration and mild sound dampening.">Lembaran coir yang dipadatkan kian banyak dipakai sebagai panel dinding dekoratif di kafe, hotel butik, hingga interior bernuansa ramah lingkungan, karena tampilan bertekstur organiknya yang sulit ditiru material sintetis. Karena bahannya ringan dan mudah dipotong, pengrajin membentuknya menjadi hiasan dinding custom, bingkai bertekstur, hingga lapisan panel akustik yang sekaligus berfungsi sebagai dekorasi dan peredam suara ringan.</p><figure class="article-figure">
<img alt="Anyaman dekoratif dari serat sabut kelapa" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1600166898405-da9535204843?w=1200&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;q=80"/>
<figcaption data-en="Coir fiber woven into a decorative panel with natural, organic texture">Serat coir dianyam menjadi panel dekoratif dengan tekstur alami yang organik</figcaption>
</figure><h2 data-en="Why Artisans Choose Coco Fiber">Mengapa Pengrajin Memilih Coco Fiber</h2><ul>
<li data-en="Naturally coarse texture with genuine handmade character">Tekstur kasar alami dengan karakter buatan tangan yang khas</li>
<li data-en="Takes dye well while retaining its organic grain">Menyerap pewarna dengan baik tanpa kehilangan serat alaminya</li>
<li data-en="Lightweight, easy to cut, weave, and shape">Ringan, mudah dipotong, dianyam, dan dibentuk</li>
<li data-en="A biodegradable alternative to plastic-based craft materials">Alternatif biodegradable pengganti bahan kerajinan berbasis plastik</li>
</ul><p data-en="For craft businesses and export buyers looking for a sustainable raw material with visual character, coco fiber offers both practicality and a story, made from coconut husk that would otherwise go to waste.">Bagi pelaku usaha kerajinan maupun buyer ekspor yang mencari bahan baku berkelanjutan dengan nilai visual, coco fiber menawarkan sisi praktis sekaligus cerita di baliknya, berasal dari sabut kelapa yang jika tidak diolah hanya akan menjadi limbah.</p> $$,$$ <h2>Woven Doormats, Rope &amp; Cordage</h2><p>Coir fiber has long been spun into rope and twine because of its natural resistance to saltwater and abrasion, historically used in maritime cordage. Today, the same durable strands are woven into doormats and floor mats prized for their coarse, slip-resistant texture, ideal for entryways that see heavy foot traffic. Artisans also braid coir into decorative rope for baskets, plant hangers, and rustic-style furniture accents.</p><p>Because the fiber holds dye well while still showing its natural grain, crafters can produce both earthy neutral pieces and vividly colored accent items from the same raw material.</p><h2>Decorative Panels &amp; Wall Art</h2><p>Compressed coir sheets are increasingly used as decorative wall panels in cafes, boutique hotels, and eco-conscious interiors, valued for their organic, textured look that synthetic materials struggle to replicate. Because the material is lightweight and easy to cut, artisans shape it into custom wall art, framed textures, and acoustic panel backing that doubles as both decoration and mild sound dampening.</p><figure class="article-figure">
<img alt="Anyaman dekoratif dari serat sabut kelapa" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1600166898405-da9535204843?w=1200&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;q=80"/>
<figcaption>Coir fiber woven into a decorative panel with natural, organic texture</figcaption>
</figure><h2>Why Artisans Choose Coco Fiber</h2><ul>
<li>Naturally coarse texture with genuine handmade character</li>
<li>Takes dye well while retaining its organic grain</li>
<li>Lightweight, easy to cut, weave, and shape</li>
<li>A biodegradable alternative to plastic-based craft materials</li>
</ul><p>For craft businesses and export buyers looking for a sustainable raw material with visual character, coco fiber offers both practicality and a story, made from coconut husk that would otherwise go to waste.</p> $$,'Kerajinan & Dekorasi','https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1622560481156-01ecc6603334?w=1400&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80','Tim CocoFiber','published','2026-08-13')
