insert into artikel (slug,judul,judul_en,ringkasan,ringkasan_en,konten,konten_en,kategori,gambar_url,penulis,status,tanggal)
values ('coco-fiber-produksi','Dari Sabut Kelapa hingga Ekspor: Proses Produksi Coco Fiber','From Coconut Husk to Export: The Coco Fiber Production Process','Di balik setiap bal coco fiber siap ekspor, ada proses bertahap yang mengubah sabut kelapa mentah, yang sering dianggap limbah pertanian, menjadi bahan baku berkualitas dan konsisten untuk industri di seluruh dunia. Memahami proses ini membantu buyer memahami mengapa kualitas dan konsistensi bisa berbeda antar pemasok.','Behind every bale of export-ready coco fiber is a multi-stage process that turns raw coconut husk, often considered agricultural waste, into a consistent, high-quality raw material for industries worldwide. Understanding this process helps buyers appreciate why quality and consistency vary between suppliers.',
$$ <h2 data-en="Husk Collection &amp; Fiber Extraction">Pengumpulan Sabut &amp; Ekstraksi Serat</h2><p data-en="The process begins with collecting mature coconut husks, typically sourced from local farmers and coconut processing centers across East Java. The husks are then decorticated, either mechanically or through a retting process, where the husk is soaked to loosen the fibrous material from the pith. Mechanical decortication, the more common method for commercial-scale production, crushes and beats the husk to separate long fiber strands from the shorter pith material, known as coco dust or cocopeat.">Proses dimulai dengan pengumpulan sabut kelapa tua, biasanya bersumber dari petani lokal dan sentra pengolahan kelapa di seluruh Jawa Timur. Sabut kemudian didekortikasi, baik secara mekanis maupun melalui proses perendaman (retting), di mana sabut direndam untuk melunakkan material berserat dari empulurnya. Dekortikasi mekanis, metode yang lebih umum untuk produksi skala komersial, menghancurkan dan memukul sabut untuk memisahkan untaian serat panjang dari material empulur yang lebih pendek, dikenal sebagai coco dust atau cocopeat.</p><h2 data-en="Washing, Drying &amp; Grading">Pencucian, Pengeringan, dan Sortasi</h2><p data-en="Once separated, the fiber is washed to remove residual dust, salts, and organic debris, an important step for buyers who require low-tannin, low-conductivity fiber for sensitive applications like horticulture. The washed fiber is then sun-dried or kiln-dried depending on weather conditions and order volume, before being graded by length, color, and coarseness. Longer, cleaner fibers are typically reserved for industrial applications such as automotive filling, while shorter or mixed-grade fiber is suited for geotextiles and bulk agricultural use.">Setelah dipisahkan, serat dicuci untuk menghilangkan sisa debu, garam, dan kotoran organik, langkah penting bagi buyer yang membutuhkan serat rendah tanin dan rendah konduktivitas untuk aplikasi sensitif seperti hortikultura. Serat yang sudah dicuci lalu dijemur atau dikeringkan dengan oven tergantung kondisi cuaca dan volume pesanan, sebelum disortir berdasarkan panjang, warna, dan kekasarannya. Serat yang lebih panjang dan bersih biasanya disisihkan untuk aplikasi industri seperti bahan pengisi otomotif, sementara serat lebih pendek atau campuran cocok untuk geotekstil dan penggunaan pertanian dalam jumlah besar.</p><figure class="article-figure">
<img alt="Serat coco fiber dijemur dalam proses produksi" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1615486364598-2e9f0e46f74f?w=1200&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;q=80"/>
<figcaption data-en="Fiber is sun-dried and graded by length and coarseness before baling">Serat dijemur dan disortir berdasarkan panjang serta kekasaran sebelum dibal</figcaption>
</figure><h2 data-en="Pressing, Baling &amp; Export Packaging">Pengepresan, Pengebalan, dan Pengemasan Ekspor</h2><p data-en="Graded fiber is compressed using hydraulic baling presses into dense, uniform bales, typically wrapped in wire or strapping to withstand handling and long-distance shipping. Compressing the fiber significantly reduces shipping volume, an important cost factor for container-based export. Each bale is weighed, labeled, and, where required, fumigated or heat-treated to meet phytosanitary import requirements before being loaded into containers bound for international buyers.">Serat yang sudah disortir dipadatkan menggunakan mesin press hidrolik menjadi bal-bal padat dan seragam, biasanya diikat kawat atau strapping agar tahan terhadap penanganan dan pengiriman jarak jauh. Pemadatan serat secara signifikan mengurangi volume pengiriman, faktor biaya penting untuk ekspor berbasis kontainer. Setiap bal ditimbang, diberi label, dan bila diperlukan, difumigasi atau diberi perlakuan panas untuk memenuhi persyaratan fitosanitasi impor sebelum dimuat ke kontainer menuju buyer internasional.</p><h2 data-en="What This Means for Buyers">Apa Artinya Bagi Buyer</h2><ul>
<li data-en="Consistent quality comes from controlled washing, drying, and grading steps">Kualitas konsisten berasal dari tahap pencucian, pengeringan, dan sortasi yang terkontrol</li>
<li data-en="Fiber grade should match the intended application, industrial vs agricultural">Grade serat harus disesuaikan dengan aplikasi yang dituju, industri vs pertanian</li>
<li data-en="Proper baling reduces shipping cost and protects fiber during transit">Pengebalan yang tepat menekan biaya pengiriman dan melindungi serat selama transit</li>
<li data-en="Phytosanitary treatment is essential for smooth customs clearance">Perlakuan fitosanitasi penting untuk kelancaran proses kepabeanan</li>
</ul><p data-en="A transparent, well-controlled production process is what separates a reliable export supplier from an inconsistent one. Buyers evaluating a coco fiber supplier should ask about each of these stages to understand the quality and consistency they can expect.">Proses produksi yang transparan dan terkontrol dengan baik adalah pembeda antara pemasok ekspor yang andal dan yang tidak konsisten. Buyer yang mengevaluasi pemasok coco fiber sebaiknya menanyakan setiap tahap ini untuk memahami kualitas dan konsistensi yang bisa diharapkan.</p> $$,$$ <h2>Husk Collection &amp; Fiber Extraction</h2><p>The process begins with collecting mature coconut husks, typically sourced from local farmers and coconut processing centers across East Java. The husks are then decorticated, either mechanically or through a retting process, where the husk is soaked to loosen the fibrous material from the pith. Mechanical decortication, the more common method for commercial-scale production, crushes and beats the husk to separate long fiber strands from the shorter pith material, known as coco dust or cocopeat.</p><h2>Washing, Drying &amp; Grading</h2><p>Once separated, the fiber is washed to remove residual dust, salts, and organic debris, an important step for buyers who require low-tannin, low-conductivity fiber for sensitive applications like horticulture. The washed fiber is then sun-dried or kiln-dried depending on weather conditions and order volume, before being graded by length, color, and coarseness. Longer, cleaner fibers are typically reserved for industrial applications such as automotive filling, while shorter or mixed-grade fiber is suited for geotextiles and bulk agricultural use.</p><figure class="article-figure">
<img alt="Serat coco fiber dijemur dalam proses produksi" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1615486364598-2e9f0e46f74f?w=1200&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;q=80"/>
<figcaption>Fiber is sun-dried and graded by length and coarseness before baling</figcaption>
</figure><h2>Pressing, Baling &amp; Export Packaging</h2><p>Graded fiber is compressed using hydraulic baling presses into dense, uniform bales, typically wrapped in wire or strapping to withstand handling and long-distance shipping. Compressing the fiber significantly reduces shipping volume, an important cost factor for container-based export. Each bale is weighed, labeled, and, where required, fumigated or heat-treated to meet phytosanitary import requirements before being loaded into containers bound for international buyers.</p><h2>What This Means for Buyers</h2><ul>
<li>Consistent quality comes from controlled washing, drying, and grading steps</li>
<li>Fiber grade should match the intended application, industrial vs agricultural</li>
<li>Proper baling reduces shipping cost and protects fiber during transit</li>
<li>Phytosanitary treatment is essential for smooth customs clearance</li>
</ul><p>A transparent, well-controlled production process is what separates a reliable export supplier from an inconsistent one. Buyers evaluating a coco fiber supplier should ask about each of these stages to understand the quality and consistency they can expect.</p> $$,'Proses Produksi','https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1595231712325-9fedb0e78f8d?w=1400&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80','Tim CocoFiber','published','2026-08-13')
