insert into artikel (slug,judul,judul_en,ringkasan,ringkasan_en,konten,konten_en,kategori,gambar_url,penulis,status,tanggal)
values ('cocopeat-perkebunan','Cocopeat untuk Perkebunan Skala Besar: Substrat Tanam Alternatif Tanah','Cocopeat for Large-Scale Plantations: An Alternative Growing Substrate','Pelaku pertanian skala besar kian banyak mengganti atau melengkapi tanah dengan cocopeat sebagai substrat tanam. Struktur yang konsisten, daya serap air unggul, dan bebas patogen bawaan tanah menjadikannya menarik bagi operasi perkebunan yang mengejar hasil panen yang lebih terprediksi.','Large-scale growers are increasingly replacing or supplementing soil with cocopeat as a growing substrate. Its consistent structure, superior water retention, and freedom from soil-borne pathogens make it attractive for plantation-scale operations aiming for predictable yields.',
$$ <h2 data-en="Consistent Structure Across Large Areas">Struktur Konsisten di Lahan Luas</h2><p data-en="Unlike field soil, which varies in composition from plot to plot, processed cocopeat offers a uniform structure and pH across every batch. For plantation operators managing hundreds of hectares, this consistency simplifies fertigation planning and reduces the guesswork involved in nutrient dosing, since the growing medium behaves the same way regardless of which block it is used in.">Berbeda dengan tanah lahan yang komposisinya bervariasi antar petak, cocopeat olahan menawarkan struktur dan pH yang seragam di setiap batch-nya. Bagi operator perkebunan yang mengelola ratusan hektare, konsistensi ini menyederhanakan perencanaan fertigasi dan mengurangi tebak-tebakan dalam dosis nutrisi, karena media tanam berperilaku sama di blok mana pun digunakan.</p><p data-en="This uniformity also makes cocopeat well suited to mechanized and semi-automated irrigation systems, where predictable water retention is critical to avoiding both under- and over-watering across large plots.">Keseragaman ini juga membuat cocopeat cocok untuk sistem irigasi mekanis maupun semi-otomatis, di mana daya serap air yang terprediksi sangat penting untuk menghindari kekurangan maupun kelebihan air di lahan yang luas.</p><h2 data-en="Reduced Disease Pressure &amp; Better Root Aeration">Tekanan Penyakit Lebih Rendah &amp; Aerasi Akar Lebih Baik</h2><p data-en="Because cocopeat is processed and largely free of soil-borne fungi, nematodes, and weed seeds, plantations using it as a substrate often see reduced disease pressure compared to open-field soil cultivation. Its airy, fibrous structure also prevents compaction, allowing roots to access oxygen even in high-density planting layouts, a common challenge in intensive plantation systems.">Karena cocopeat diproses dan relatif bebas dari jamur, nematoda, serta biji gulma yang biasa terbawa tanah, perkebunan yang menggunakannya sebagai substrat sering kali mengalami tekanan penyakit yang lebih rendah dibanding budidaya tanah terbuka. Struktur berseratnya yang berongga juga mencegah pemadatan, sehingga akar tetap mendapat oksigen meski di tata letak tanam berkepadatan tinggi, tantangan umum pada sistem perkebunan intensif.</p><figure class="article-figure">
<img alt="Cocopeat digunakan sebagai substrat tanam perkebunan" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1592982537447-7440770cbfc9?w=1200&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;q=80"/>
<figcaption data-en="Cocopeat substrate provides consistent structure across large planting areas">Substrat cocopeat memberikan struktur konsisten di lahan tanam yang luas</figcaption>
</figure><h2 data-en="Why Plantations Choose Cocopeat">Mengapa Perkebunan Memilih Cocopeat</h2><ul>
<li data-en="Uniform structure and pH across every batch">Struktur dan pH seragam di setiap batch</li>
<li data-en="Excellent water retention, reducing irrigation frequency">Daya serap air unggul, mengurangi frekuensi irigasi</li>
<li data-en="Largely free of soil-borne pathogens and weed seeds">Relatif bebas patogen bawaan tanah dan biji gulma</li>
<li data-en="Renewable, biodegradable alternative to peat moss">Alternatif terbarukan dan biodegradable pengganti peat moss</li>
</ul><p data-en="As plantation operators look for ways to standardize yields and reduce dependency on variable field soil, cocopeat offers a scalable, renewable substrate suited to modern, high-density cultivation.">Seiring operator perkebunan mencari cara menstandarkan hasil panen dan mengurangi ketergantungan pada tanah lahan yang bervariasi, cocopeat menawarkan substrat yang scalable dan terbarukan, sesuai untuk budidaya modern berkepadatan tinggi.</p> $$,$$ <h2>Consistent Structure Across Large Areas</h2><p>Unlike field soil, which varies in composition from plot to plot, processed cocopeat offers a uniform structure and pH across every batch. For plantation operators managing hundreds of hectares, this consistency simplifies fertigation planning and reduces the guesswork involved in nutrient dosing, since the growing medium behaves the same way regardless of which block it is used in.</p><p>This uniformity also makes cocopeat well suited to mechanized and semi-automated irrigation systems, where predictable water retention is critical to avoiding both under- and over-watering across large plots.</p><h2>Reduced Disease Pressure &amp; Better Root Aeration</h2><p>Because cocopeat is processed and largely free of soil-borne fungi, nematodes, and weed seeds, plantations using it as a substrate often see reduced disease pressure compared to open-field soil cultivation. Its airy, fibrous structure also prevents compaction, allowing roots to access oxygen even in high-density planting layouts, a common challenge in intensive plantation systems.</p><figure class="article-figure">
<img alt="Cocopeat digunakan sebagai substrat tanam perkebunan" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1592982537447-7440770cbfc9?w=1200&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;q=80"/>
<figcaption>Cocopeat substrate provides consistent structure across large planting areas</figcaption>
</figure><h2>Why Plantations Choose Cocopeat</h2><ul>
<li>Uniform structure and pH across every batch</li>
<li>Excellent water retention, reducing irrigation frequency</li>
<li>Largely free of soil-borne pathogens and weed seeds</li>
<li>Renewable, biodegradable alternative to peat moss</li>
</ul><p>As plantation operators look for ways to standardize yields and reduce dependency on variable field soil, cocopeat offers a scalable, renewable substrate suited to modern, high-density cultivation.</p> $$,'Pertanian & Perkebunan','https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1625246333195-78d9c38ad449?w=1400&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80','Tim CocoFiber','published','2026-08-13')
