insert into artikel (slug,judul,judul_en,ringkasan,ringkasan_en,konten,konten_en,kategori,gambar_url,penulis,status,tanggal)
values ('cocopot-cocodisc-pembibitan','Cocopot & Cocodisc: Solusi Ramah Lingkungan Pengganti Polybag','Cocopot & Cocodisc: An Eco-Friendly Alternative to Polybags','Polybag plastik selama ini menjadi wadah standar untuk pembibitan tanaman, namun meninggalkan limbah plastik permanen setelah bibit dipindah tanam. Cocopot dan cocodisc, berbahan serat kelapa padat, menawarkan alternatif biodegradable yang bisa langsung ditanam ke tanah bersama potnya.','Plastic polybags have long been the default container for seedling nurseries, but they leave lasting plastic waste once seedlings are transplanted. Cocopot and cocodisc, made from compressed coconut fiber, offer a biodegradable alternative that can be planted directly into the ground, pot and all.',
$$ <h2 data-en="Plant Directly, No Transplant Shock">Tanam Langsung, Tanpa Stres Pindah Tanam</h2><p data-en="One of the biggest advantages of cocopot over polybags is that seedlings can be planted directly into the ground without removing them from their container. Because the pot itself is biodegradable coconut fiber, roots simply grow through it as it breaks down, eliminating the root disturbance and transplant shock that often occurs when seedlings are pulled from plastic bags. This is particularly valuable for reforestation and greening projects, where survival rates matter as much as planting volume.">Salah satu keunggulan utama cocopot dibanding polybag adalah bibit bisa langsung ditanam ke tanah tanpa perlu dikeluarkan dari wadahnya. Karena potnya sendiri berbahan serat kelapa biodegradable, akar tumbuh menembus wadah seiring terurainya material, sehingga menghilangkan gangguan akar dan stres pindah tanam yang sering terjadi saat bibit dicabut dari kantong plastik. Ini sangat berguna untuk proyek reboisasi dan penghijauan, di mana tingkat keberhasilan tumbuh sama pentingnya dengan volume penanaman.</p><h2 data-en="Cocodisc for Compact, High-Density Nurseries">Cocodisc untuk Pembibitan Kompak Berkepadatan Tinggi</h2><p data-en="Cocodisc, a flatter, compressed coir disc, is designed for nurseries that need to germinate large volumes of seedlings in limited space. Dry and lightweight before use, cocodiscs expand once hydrated, expanding into a compact growing block that takes up far less storage and shipping space than pre-filled polybags. This makes them practical for large-scale reforestation programs and nurseries that need to transport thousands of starter units efficiently.">Cocodisc, cakram coir padat yang lebih tipis, dirancang untuk pembibitan yang perlu menyemai bibit dalam volume besar dengan ruang terbatas. Kering dan ringan sebelum digunakan, cocodisc mengembang setelah dihidrasi menjadi blok tanam padat yang jauh lebih hemat ruang penyimpanan dan pengiriman dibanding polybag yang sudah terisi tanah. Ini membuatnya praktis untuk program reboisasi skala besar dan pembibitan yang perlu mengangkut ribuan unit starter secara efisien.</p><figure class="article-figure">
<img alt="Bibit tanaman di pembibitan menggunakan cocodisc" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1466692476868-aef1dfb1e735?w=1200&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;q=80"/>
<figcaption data-en="Cocodisc expands into a compact growing block once hydrated, ideal for high-volume nurseries">Cocodisc mengembang menjadi blok tanam padat setelah dihidrasi, ideal untuk pembibitan volume tinggi</figcaption>
</figure><h2 data-en="Why Nurseries Are Switching from Polybags">Mengapa Pembibitan Beralih dari Polybag</h2><ul>
<li data-en="Plant directly into soil, container included, no transplant shock">Tanam langsung ke tanah beserta wadahnya, tanpa stres pindah tanam</li>
<li data-en="Fully biodegradable, leaves no plastic waste in the field">Sepenuhnya biodegradable, tidak meninggalkan limbah plastik di lahan</li>
<li data-en="Compact, lightweight storage and shipping before hydration">Penyimpanan dan pengiriman kompak serta ringan sebelum dihidrasi</li>
<li data-en="Custom sizing available for different seedling types">Ukuran custom tersedia untuk berbagai jenis bibit</li>
</ul><p data-en="For reforestation programs, plantation nurseries, and greening initiatives looking to reduce plastic waste without compromising seedling survival rates, cocopot and cocodisc offer a practical, field-proven alternative.">Bagi program reboisasi, pembibitan perkebunan, dan inisiatif penghijauan yang ingin mengurangi limbah plastik tanpa mengorbankan tingkat keberhasilan tumbuh bibit, cocopot dan cocodisc menawarkan alternatif praktis yang telah terbukti di lapangan.</p> $$,$$ <h2>Plant Directly, No Transplant Shock</h2><p>One of the biggest advantages of cocopot over polybags is that seedlings can be planted directly into the ground without removing them from their container. Because the pot itself is biodegradable coconut fiber, roots simply grow through it as it breaks down, eliminating the root disturbance and transplant shock that often occurs when seedlings are pulled from plastic bags. This is particularly valuable for reforestation and greening projects, where survival rates matter as much as planting volume.</p><h2>Cocodisc for Compact, High-Density Nurseries</h2><p>Cocodisc, a flatter, compressed coir disc, is designed for nurseries that need to germinate large volumes of seedlings in limited space. Dry and lightweight before use, cocodiscs expand once hydrated, expanding into a compact growing block that takes up far less storage and shipping space than pre-filled polybags. This makes them practical for large-scale reforestation programs and nurseries that need to transport thousands of starter units efficiently.</p><figure class="article-figure">
<img alt="Bibit tanaman di pembibitan menggunakan cocodisc" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1466692476868-aef1dfb1e735?w=1200&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;q=80"/>
<figcaption>Cocodisc expands into a compact growing block once hydrated, ideal for high-volume nurseries</figcaption>
</figure><h2>Why Nurseries Are Switching from Polybags</h2><ul>
<li>Plant directly into soil, container included, no transplant shock</li>
<li>Fully biodegradable, leaves no plastic waste in the field</li>
<li>Compact, lightweight storage and shipping before hydration</li>
<li>Custom sizing available for different seedling types</li>
</ul><p>For reforestation programs, plantation nurseries, and greening initiatives looking to reduce plastic waste without compromising seedling survival rates, cocopot and cocodisc offer a practical, field-proven alternative.</p> $$,'Pembibitan','https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1585687433492-9c648106f131?w=1400&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80','Tim CocoFiber','published','2026-08-13')
